# Seiche's speed dial (physics catalog plan, 2026-10-03): fast-forward under
# the frame budget, half the display's frame period (ruled 2026-10-04,
# "Target + Max, budget as frame share", "The display's frame"), never more
# than half of 1/60 s on the web ("Known rate, else capped"), the gate keeping
# 200 us past the forecast tick ("Gate keeps a forecast margin").
# tree.html?nodes=300&seed=7&links=none&gpu=off&physics_speed=max runs as fast
# as the budget allows, so the budget binds every frame, the canvas reports
# the speed it reached, and stepping stays inside each frame's own budget.
# p6_tree_speed_fast_control is 50x at 24 nodes.
assert snap ready == true
assert snap physics-speed == max
assert snap physics-budget-share == 0.5
assert snap physics-budget-margin-us == 200
click role:button Play physics
settle 2
assert snap physics-paused == false
click role:combobox Arrangement
settle 1
click role:option Free (physics alone)
settle 1
click role:button Apply arrangement
settle 1
assert snap layout == free
settle 10
timing start speed-fast
settle 30
timing stop
log-physics fast
log-pace fast
assert snap physics-budget-bound == true
assert snap physics-effective-speed >= 1
assert snap pace-frames == 30
# The 300-node page is far slower than its display: the period is capped.
assert snap display-period-ms <= 16.7
assert snap physics-budget-us <= 8333
# Each frame's bound is its budget plus the browser clock's 100 us
# resolution (performance.now), ruled 2026-10-04, "Bound = budget + clock
# grain", over every frame above real time since the page opened, not only
# the last window's (ruled the same day with the margin).
assert snap pace-over-budget-us <= 100
assert snap pace-over-budget-worst-us <= 100
assert snap pace-over-grain-frames == 0
assert snap finite == true
log p6 speed fast receipt complete
